<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="The totals">
        <FluentText>
            The boxes at the top of the Day and Week views add up every party that isn't cancelled:
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Parties</strong>, <strong>children</strong> and <strong>adults</strong> expected. A private hire counts its
                guests as children.</li>
            <li><strong>Hot / cold food</strong>: how many parties are having the hot food sheet and how many the cold one, so the
                kitchen knows what's coming. Private hires have no party food.</li>
            <li><strong>Not paid in full</strong>: parties that are unpaid or have only paid the deposit, with the balance still due
                where the price is known.</li>
            <li><strong>Provisional</strong>, when there are any: holds from Just Step Online that aren't confirmed yet.</li>
            <li>On the Day view, <strong>staff on</strong>: how many people are on the published rota that day.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Staff on shift">
        <FluentText>
            Beside the timeline (under the parties on a phone) is everyone on the published rota that day, earliest start first,
            with their times and position. The coloured dot is the position's colour from the <a href="/manage/rota">rota</a>.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            Only published shifts appear, as the staff were last told them. Drafts and changes you haven't published yet don't
            show here, and neither do open shifts with nobody on them.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
